**What is content negotiation ?
Content Negotiation is a mechanism in REST APIs where the client and server agree on the format of the request or response data.
Client send "Accept: application/json" in header.
what type of data present in request body - "Content-Type: application/json" .
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

builder.Services
    .AddControllers(options =>
    {
        // Return 406 if requested format isn't supported
        options.ReturnHttpNotAcceptable = true;
    })
    .AddXmlSerializerFormatters(); // register XML format. json format is registered by default


**Difference Run(), Map(), and Use() in .Net core
Use()	Adds middleware to the pipeline. allows you to execute some logic before and after the next middleware.
Map()	Creates a separate pipeline for a matching path
Run()	Adds terminal middleware

app.Use(async (context, next) =>
{
    Console.WriteLine("Before middleware");

    await next();

    Console.WriteLine("After middleware");
});

Map() creates a separate middleware pipeline based on the request path.
app.Map("/admin", adminApp =>
{
    adminApp.Run(async context =>
    {
        await context.Response.WriteAsync("Admin section");
    });
});

Map() branches based on a URL path.
MapWhen() branches based on a custom condition (predicate) on HttpContext.

app.MapWhen(
    context => context.Request.Headers.ContainsKey("X-Custom-Header"),
    branch =>
    {
        branch.Run(async context =>
        {
            await context.Response.WriteAsync("Custom header found");
        });
    });











